      "title": "New Knesset speaker could be key to ousting Netanyahu as Israel’s PM",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/nov/10/new-knesset-speaker-ousting-netanyahu-israel-pm",
      "description": "<p>Opposition politicians get first chance to take control of levers of power, even as they struggle to form government</p><p>Israel’s new Knesset will be sworn in on Tuesday, giving opposition politicians their first chance to take control of some levers of power, even as they struggle to form a new government to unseat Benjamin Netanyahu.</p><p>High on the agenda will be replacing the speaker, who wields immense influence by controlling the legislature’s agenda and committee chairs. The current speaker is Amir Ohana, a close ally of Netanyahu.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/nov/10/new-knesset-speaker-ousting-netanyahu-israel-pm\">Continue reading...</a>",
